# The original test files are hash-pinned at kickoff. CRLF normalisation would
# change their sha256 and break the contract with the judges. Force LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.wasm binary

# tests/original/ is upstream's test suite, copied in byte for byte and hash
# pinned. It is vendored in the literal sense the attribute means: not written
# here, and not modifiable without breaking the contract with the judges.
# Marking it keeps GitHub's language bar describing the code this project
# actually wrote.
#
# Deliberately scoped to that directory alone. adapter/, bridge/, fuzz/, bench/
# and compare/ are TypeScript and JavaScript written for this port, and they
# stay counted: a Go port that needed a WebAssembly bridge and a JS-side
# harness to prove itself is honest signal about what the work involved, not
# something to tidy out of the statistics.
tests/original/** linguist-vendored
